WEBVTT

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:04.440
Arihara Tsubasa here.

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:07.610
Give me a sitrep, please. Over.

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:09.310
This is Nozaki.

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:12.070
Sadly, it looks like the school ground
is out of the question.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.990
No luck with the gym, either.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:23.660
Doesn't look like the judo hall
will work, either...

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:27.880
<i>I don't think it's possible to
play baseball in a judo hall, anyway.</i>

00:00:29.890 --> 00:00:31.990
Isn't there anywhere else?

00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:36.180
Arihara here! Target located!

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:45.100
Girls'
Baseball
Association

00:00:39.650 --> 00:00:45.100
Okay, this is where the girls' 
baseball association will practice!

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:48.560
Are you sure it's all right?

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:52.070
Won't the student council
chew us out again if they find out?

00:00:52.070 --> 00:00:53.630
It'll be fi—

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:54.710
Who authorized this?

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.200
Um, well...

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:02.700
I will have to inform
the student council president of this.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:06.620
I'm sorry!

00:01:07.970 --> 00:01:12.380
Well, it would indeed be dangerous 
if a ball were to break a window.

00:01:15.070 --> 00:01:18.300
Why can't we practice here at school?

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:24.810
This school already has twenty athletic clubs
and fifteen cultural clubs.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:29.060
In addition, the sport of baseball
requires extensive facilities and equipment,

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:31.720
and there is no appropriate
location on this campus.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:35.870
Then, we'll find a place ourselves.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.450
What should we do?

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:21.970
<b>Can or Can't</b>

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.470
Satogahama Baseball

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:23.890
Satogahama Baseball

00:03:23.480 --> 00:03:26.310
This is... a baseball shop?

00:03:23.890 --> 00:03:24.600
Satogahama Baseball

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.310
Yeah! I come here all the time.

00:03:28.310 --> 00:03:30.080
If you need baseball equipment,

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:34.560
come to the cheap and trustworthy kings of
customer service, Satogahama Baseball!

00:03:34.560 --> 00:03:38.330
We borrowed the gloves we used
at the trial meet-up from here, too.

00:03:38.330 --> 00:03:40.030
Ah, I see.

00:03:40.030 --> 00:03:42.780
We still need to find a place to practice,

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.630
but let's take it one step at a time.

00:03:44.630 --> 00:03:46.620
And you all need gloves, right?

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:48.080
Gloves...

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:50.080
I want one!

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:49.450
Satogahama Baseball

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:49.870
Satogahama Baseball

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:50.080
Satogahama Baseball

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:57.750
I didn't realize baseball had
such a range of equipment...

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:02.510
Yeah. Gloves are even shaped differently,
depending on your position.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:08.300
But since we haven't decided
what positions we're playing yet,

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:11.270
we're buying these all-rounder gloves today.

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.690
Thirty thousand...

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.290
Fifty thousand...

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:23.110
Seventy thousand?!

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:29.510
Gloves are pretty expensive, huh?

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:30.730
Not to worry!

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:34.540
Boss, could you show us 
those things I asked for?

00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:34.790
2,000 Yen Each

00:04:34.790 --> 00:04:34.920
2,000 Yen Each

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:35.040
2,000 Yen Each

00:04:34.990 --> 00:04:36.060
Sure thing.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:35.170
2,000 Yen Each

00:04:35.170 --> 00:04:35.290
2,000 Yen Each

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:35.370
2,000 Yen Each

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:35.460
2,000 Yen Each

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:36.670
2,000 Yen Each

00:04:36.670 --> 00:04:38.830
They're pretty old and out-of-date,

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:41.070
but with a little TLC, they're usable.

00:04:42.130 --> 00:04:43.800
<b>2,000 Yen Each</b>

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.350
Two thousand yen...

00:04:45.350 --> 00:04:47.110
Go on, pick one out!

00:04:47.110 --> 00:04:49.990
Um, how do we choose the right one?

00:04:49.990 --> 00:04:52.660
The most important thing
is the feeling it gives you.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:54.220
It should give you a jolt!

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:55.390
A jolt?

00:04:55.810 --> 00:05:00.390
Each glove differs in weight, 
center of gravity, and size.

00:05:00.390 --> 00:05:03.820
Just try some on, and pick 
the one that feels right.

00:05:03.820 --> 00:05:05.310
What he said!

00:05:05.310 --> 00:05:07.070
I see.

00:05:07.400 --> 00:05:09.870
Do you have any for left-handers?

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:11.770
A lighter glove might be 
better for you, Ukita-san.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:13.020
Just a sec. We should have a few.

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:13.020
How about this one?

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:13.520
Okay.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:17.150
Let's see... Ah, here we go.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:16.250
Okay. I'll try it.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.290
It's perfect.

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:22.610
Suzuki-san?

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:23.920
Nozaki-san...

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.570
What a coincidence.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:29.890
Hey, Suzuki-san, does this mean 
you're interested in baseball?

00:05:31.470 --> 00:05:33.420
Is she from our school?

00:05:33.420 --> 00:05:34.430
Seems like it...

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:36.620
I'm just accompanying someone.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.110
What's up, Waka?

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:47.140
I-Is he your boyf—

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:48.990
No. He's my older brother.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:51.070
Hello.

00:05:53.080 --> 00:05:56.960
What?! Your brother plays 
for Takuhou University?!

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:55.290
<b>Tetsujin
Chinese Cuisine</b>

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:55.290
<b>Gyoza              Ramen 
Chukadon   Meat Buns</b>

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:56.250
<b>Tetsujin
Chinese Cuisine</b>

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:56.250
<b>Gyoza              Ramen 
Chukadon   Meat Buns</b>

00:05:56.960 --> 00:05:58.650
Is it famous?

00:05:58.650 --> 00:06:00.610
It's a college baseball powerhouse.

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.530
Thank you for waiting!

00:06:06.010 --> 00:06:07.880
It looks so good!

00:06:07.880 --> 00:06:10.000
Eat as much as you want.

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.890
Call it a thank-you for
looking out for my kid sister.

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.810
Thank you!

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:17.520
They don't look out for me...

00:06:17.930 --> 00:06:21.480
And this is a special serving 
of our signature fried rice.

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:25.280
But we didn't order this...

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:26.900
It's on the house.

00:06:26.900 --> 00:06:30.240
Eat your fill and work hard, 
future baseball team!

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.200
Wait, did you go to the same school as us?

00:06:33.550 --> 00:06:34.910
Enjoy your meal.

00:06:34.910 --> 00:06:36.910
Thank you!

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.120
Let's eat!

00:06:43.820 --> 00:06:48.840
By the way, Arihara-san,
you bought lots of things at that shop.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.050
Yeah! I got these.

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:52.760
What are those?

00:06:52.760 --> 00:06:54.550
Well, they're...

00:06:55.190 --> 00:06:57.150
Glove oil and a glove mallet.

00:06:58.970 --> 00:07:01.690
You use them to shape tough gloves.

00:07:01.690 --> 00:07:03.190
Shape them?

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.400
Yes, you work the leather
to fit the shape of your hand.

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:08.110
Ah...

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:15.640
Suzuki-san, since you know so much about it,

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:18.200
does that mean you
actually kinda like baseball?

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:22.380
If you do, please play baseball with us!

00:07:23.190 --> 00:07:24.600
I'll pass.

00:07:27.340 --> 00:07:29.990
I don't play baseball.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:34.640
What about a support role?

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.260
Hey! Onii-chan!

00:07:37.260 --> 00:07:41.570
You helped out my team when
I played little league, remember?

00:07:42.190 --> 00:07:44.580
You came up with
practice regimens and strategies,

00:07:44.580 --> 00:07:47.480
kept scorebooks, and took care of our gear.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:49.540
You were a huge help.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:59.030
I'll think about it.

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.670
One Pitch
With All Your Soul

00:08:04.220 --> 00:08:06.920
Um... Suzuki-san?

00:08:07.630 --> 00:08:11.570
Could you teach us how to shape our gloves?

00:08:11.570 --> 00:08:16.350
Yeah, I tried to explain how to, 
but it didn't really work.

00:08:16.350 --> 00:08:18.680
Why does that mean I have to do it?

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:22.140
We're all part of the baseball 
association, aren't we?

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:24.600
I haven't made up my mind on that.

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.600
Baseball Gorou

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.600
<b>First-Round
Draft Picks</b>

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:24.600
<b>Feature:
What to Expect</b>

00:08:24.990 --> 00:08:27.210
But you're <i>practically</i> part 
of the baseball association!

00:08:30.200 --> 00:08:33.220
Start by spraying the oil onto the glove,

00:08:33.220 --> 00:08:38.280
then pound the spot between the index 
finger and thumb with the mallet.

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:41.220
That'll make it easier to catch the ball.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:42.680
Wow, check that out.

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:44.710
Rookies?

00:08:45.700 --> 00:08:46.680
Thanks!

00:08:46.680 --> 00:08:47.540
Thank you!

00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:49.690
Thank you for your help.

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:50.950
Thanks!

00:08:50.950 --> 00:08:51.990
Arihara-san.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:56.340
Are you the only member who's played before?

00:08:56.340 --> 00:08:57.860
Yeah, I am.

00:08:57.860 --> 00:08:59.340
Are you okay with that?

00:09:00.530 --> 00:09:01.830
Of course!

00:09:07.310 --> 00:09:09.250
What else will we need?

00:09:08.260 --> 00:09:10.420
Arihara-san! Kawakita-san!

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:10.110
Yeah...

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:12.350
Sensei?

00:09:12.350 --> 00:09:16.640
I found a place for you 
to practice baseball.

00:09:16.640 --> 00:09:19.150
It's an old ball field.

00:09:19.150 --> 00:09:22.370
I asked the owner
and got the okay to use it.

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:24.620
Really?

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:30.170
Seriously, I...

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:31.400
Aw, come on.

00:09:31.400 --> 00:09:35.380
I need to go to the kendo club's
practice session soon,

00:09:35.380 --> 00:09:39.530
so I'll head back after
I've introduced you to the owner.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:41.000
Will you be okay?

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:43.430
Sure. Thank you for doing this.

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:47.360
Don't mention it.
I said I'd support you, didn't I?

00:09:47.360 --> 00:09:48.650
Sensei!

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:51.460
Okay, here we are.

00:09:54.580 --> 00:09:56.070
Th-This is...

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:01.030
...the field?

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:05.550
It used to be a lovely place,

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:08.710
but lack of use turned it
into what you see now.

00:10:09.180 --> 00:10:10.970
This is the owner, Hinata-san.

00:10:10.970 --> 00:10:12.350
Hello.

00:10:12.350 --> 00:10:15.670
The field maintenance tools
should still be usable, at least.

00:10:21.010 --> 00:10:23.130
Thank you very much!

00:10:23.130 --> 00:10:26.640
Not at all. I'm just happy to see it used.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:28.440
Don't work too hard, okay?

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:33.230
Are you really going to clean this field up?

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.850
No way around it!

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:55.210
Misaki
Fighters

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:59.680
Misaki
Fighters

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:03.910
Go for it!

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:18.610
I feel like this is never going to end.

00:11:18.610 --> 00:11:21.400
We'll be the weeding 
association for a while.

00:11:21.400 --> 00:11:23.950
But it does look a lot better now.

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:28.910
Suzuki-san? Are you all right?

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.820
Huh? Yes.

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:35.150
You must be exhausted.
Why don't we finish up tomorrow?

00:11:35.150 --> 00:11:36.340
Yeah.

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:39.290
Ukita-san, let's head home.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.290
<i>That field... So it really was...</i>

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:15.040
Satogahama Baseball

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:17.150
Here's an old used backstop.

00:12:17.150 --> 00:12:18.710
Thank you!

00:12:42.400 --> 00:12:46.890
<b>One Week Later</b>

00:12:48.370 --> 00:12:50.830
The time has finally come!

00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:52.310
Here we go!

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:04.820
Here it comes!

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:08.720
I caught it!

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:10.290
Nice catch!

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.410
Looking good, Ukita-san!

00:13:21.480 --> 00:13:22.780
<i>Not even close.</i>

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:23.940
Suzuki-san?

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:30.330
Um... When I catch the ball, it doesn't make
that "thunk" noise like Nozaki-san's does.

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.160
What am I doing wrong?

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:36.660
You formed a pocket in your glove 
when you shaped it, right?

00:13:36.660 --> 00:13:38.760
You need to catch it in that.

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:41.340
In the pocket?

00:13:41.340 --> 00:13:45.800
Keep an eye on your partner,
and make sure your palm's facing the ball.

00:13:45.800 --> 00:13:48.050
It might hurt a bit, but you can catch it.

00:13:48.530 --> 00:13:50.380
Palm facing the ball...

00:13:55.930 --> 00:13:56.770
Ow!

00:13:57.160 --> 00:13:59.230
Ukita-san! Are you all right?

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:00.690
Yeah.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:04.290
<i>Ow...</i>

00:14:07.270 --> 00:14:08.430
Suzuki-san!

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:11.910
Do you want to have a little go?

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:15.330
What do you say?

00:14:19.260 --> 00:14:22.870
I can't. I told you, I don't play.

00:14:25.050 --> 00:14:26.600
Suzuki-san!

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:37.760
Onii-chan, I wanna play baseball, too!

00:14:37.760 --> 00:14:40.170
Okay. Wanna join the team?

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:50.570
Let's try our best.

00:14:53.030 --> 00:14:53.830
Yeah!

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:58.790
One, two, three, four...

00:15:16.840 --> 00:15:17.820
Here it comes!

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:21.600
Ow!

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.690
You okay, Waka?

00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:49.130
Goodness, look at those injuries.

00:15:49.130 --> 00:15:51.980
<i>I was nothing like that girl.</i>

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.540
<i>Nor like anyone else...</i>

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:57.680
Team

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:57.680
<b>Misaki
Fighters</b>

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:57.680
<b>Kaibuchi
Challengers</b>

00:15:57.300 --> 00:15:59.430
You can do it!

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:02.050
You got this!

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:07.730
Strike!

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:11.560
Strike three! You're out!

00:16:18.860 --> 00:16:19.870
I'm ready.

00:16:19.870 --> 00:16:22.290
Huh? The pitcher...

00:16:22.290 --> 00:16:23.220
What is it?

00:16:23.220 --> 00:16:25.160
Well, um...

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:32.260
Yes!

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:37.880
Ken-chan's little sister
spotted their pitcher's tell!

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:40.180
Wow, that's impressive.

00:16:44.480 --> 00:16:47.150
<b>Baseball Coaches' Association
</b>Baseball Tactics: Using the Latest Data

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:52.330
<i>I get it. I'm better at this sort of thing.</i>

00:16:58.860 --> 00:17:01.450
<i>In that case, I won't...</i>

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:20.140
Waka.

00:17:21.500 --> 00:17:22.910
Heading back to the dorm?

00:17:22.910 --> 00:17:26.190
Yeah. I'll probably be back 
home again in two weeks.

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:28.770
Okay. See you then.

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:29.580
Yep.

00:17:30.650 --> 00:17:33.690
Oh, how'd it go with
that baseball association?

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:35.540
I'm not sure.

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:38.960
I think I'll come up with
a practice regimen, at least,

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:40.740
but they're all newbies.

00:17:42.010 --> 00:17:44.500
Yeah? In that case...

00:17:45.650 --> 00:17:47.710
You should practice with them.

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:53.300
I guess you can't use your old glove...

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:56.220
N-No, I can't. You know I—

00:17:57.010 --> 00:18:01.470
You can borrow it.
Buy one for yourself later, okay?

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:03.860
Wait... Onii-chan...

00:18:18.840 --> 00:18:20.350
Here it comes, Ukita-san!

00:18:20.350 --> 00:18:21.140
Okay!

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:29.630
Need a break?

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:32.310
No need to push yourself.

00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:33.590
O-Okay...

00:18:34.620 --> 00:18:36.090
Suzuki-san?

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:37.870
What brings you here?

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:39.250
I could ask you the same thing.

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:41.730
We stayed behind to practice.

00:18:41.730 --> 00:18:44.380
I-I asked her to help me!

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:46.470
I see.

00:18:46.490 --> 00:18:47.560
Wait...

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:49.810
Did you come here to play catch?

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:52.190
Th-This is...

00:18:54.020 --> 00:18:55.730
All right! Let's do it!

00:18:55.730 --> 00:18:57.690
Wait! Listen to me!

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:00.410
Suzuki-san! Hurry!

00:19:00.780 --> 00:19:01.550
Here.

00:19:29.460 --> 00:19:31.910
<i>The more I do this, the more I realize...</i>

00:19:35.490 --> 00:19:39.140
<i>I can't do it like that.</i>

00:19:42.090 --> 00:19:43.130
<i>I...</i>

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:47.120
<i>I can't be like all of you.</i>

00:19:51.720 --> 00:19:54.580
<i>You could never understand.</i>

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:59.550
You okay? Are you tired?

00:20:00.530 --> 00:20:02.010
Maybe.

00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:04.950
Okay, I'll take over.

00:20:05.720 --> 00:20:06.940
Sure.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:09.420
You did great. I'm ready!

00:20:18.330 --> 00:20:20.400
D-Did I do something weird?

00:20:20.400 --> 00:20:22.460
Huh? No...

00:20:24.300 --> 00:20:26.700
Hey... Do you enjoy it?

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:28.870
Yeah!

00:20:32.750 --> 00:20:35.760
I was afraid of the ball at first,

00:20:35.760 --> 00:20:38.060
but I'm more used to it now.

00:20:38.060 --> 00:20:40.460
And it makes me really happy
when I catch it.

00:20:41.080 --> 00:20:43.910
Even though... it's not your forte?

00:20:45.930 --> 00:20:48.180
That doesn't even matter!

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:53.600
You like baseball, don't you, Suzuki-san?

00:20:54.620 --> 00:20:57.160
Then, you should play with us!

00:20:59.670 --> 00:21:02.860
Even I... can have fun playing?

00:21:03.300 --> 00:21:04.300
Of course!

00:21:05.250 --> 00:21:06.050
Yeah!

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:12.020
Nice throw!

00:21:12.020 --> 00:21:13.800
Here it comes, Ukita-san!

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:18.270
Suzuki-san!

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:23.330
Here goes!

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:31.970
Membership
Application

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:33.890
Membership
Application

00:21:32.410 --> 00:21:33.370
Please take it.

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:36.740
Welcome, Suzuki-san!

00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:37.850
H-Hey!

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:39.860
Now we have five.

00:21:39.860 --> 00:21:42.180
Yeah! We can finally be an associ—

00:21:42.180 --> 00:21:45.110
No, we can't. We still don't have an advisor.

00:21:45.110 --> 00:21:48.580
Oh! That's right!

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:50.660
There's an advisor right here.

00:21:52.460 --> 00:21:53.580
Surprised?

00:21:53.580 --> 00:21:57.080
I'll be advising two clubs at once,
but if you don't mind that, I want to help.

00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:59.170
Sensei!

00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:00.840
Thank you so much!

00:22:00.840 --> 00:22:02.430
Well, I'm going home.

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:07.210
Y-You're not going to practice with us?

00:22:07.800 --> 00:22:09.930
I can't today, because...

00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:13.780
I have to go buy myself a new glove.

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:20.020
<b>Next Time</b>

00:22:15.020 --> 00:22:20.020
<b>Let's Work Up a Good Sweat</b>
